description: |
    New ``jira`` export and report plugins allow synchronizing
    test metadata and results with a Jira instance.

    Use ``tmt tests export --how jira`` to create or update
    ``Test Case`` work items in a Jira project from fmf metadata.
    Credentials are provided via ``--jira-url``, ``--jira-user``
    and ``--jira-token`` options or the corresponding
    ``TMT_PLUGIN_EXPORT_JIRA_*`` environment variables. Use
    ``--create`` to create new test cases and ``--link-jira`` to
    write the Jira issue URL back into the fmf ``link`` section
    as an ``implements`` relation for future lookups.

    .. code-block:: shell

        tmt tests export --how jira --create --link-jira \
            --jira-url https://issues.redhat.com \
            --jira-user me@example.com --jira-token TOKEN \
            --project-id RHELTEST

    Use ``tmt run report --how jira`` to post test execution
    results as comments on ``Test Result`` subtasks grouped by
    distro version and, when the fmf test metadata defines a
    ``component``, by package NVR as well. The distro version and
    architecture are read from guest ``os-release`` facts. The
    package NVR is queried from the guest's package manager (``rpm``
    or ``apt``) using the test ``component`` key; results without a
    component are grouped by distro version only. Credentials are
    required the same way
    as for the export plugin, but without the ``jira-`` option
    prefix: ``url``, ``user`` and ``token`` (or the corresponding
    ``TMT_PLUGIN_REPORT_JIRA_*`` environment variables) together
    with ``project-id`` are all mandatory.

    .. code-block:: yaml

        report:
            how: jira
            url: https://issues.redhat.com
            user: me@example.com
            token: <token>
            project-id: RHELTEST
            compose-id: RHEL-10.3-20260817.0
